    <string name="wisdom_title_ayah">Verse of the Day</string>
    <string name="wisdom_title_hadith">Hadith of the Day</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_1">Indeed, prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_1">Surah An-Nisa, Verse 103</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_2">The most beloved deed to Allah is performing prayer at its stated time.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_2">Bukhari, Mawaqit 5; Muslim, Iman 137</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_3">Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_3">Surah Hud, Verse 114</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_4">The key to Paradise is prayer, and the key to prayer is ablution.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_4">Tirmidhi, Taharah 1</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_5">Unquestionably, by the remembrance of Allah hearts are assured.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_5">Surah Ar-Ra\'d, Verse 28</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_6">The five daily prayers are an expiation for what occurs between them, as long as major sins are avoided.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_6">Muslim, Taharah 16</string>
    <string name="wisdom_text_7">And seek help through patience and prayer; indeed, it is difficult except for the humbly submissive.</string>
    <string name="wisdom_source_7">Surah Al-Baqarah, Verse 45</string>

